<title>CANADA: Canada Nov wages/salaries rise over month.</title>
<headline>Canada Nov wages/salaries rise over month.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada's seasonally adjusted estimates of labor income:</p>
<p>				   Nov	    Oct	Pct change</p>
<p>    Wages and salaries  C$31.67 bln  C$31.46 bln   +0.7</p>
<p>    Labor income	  C$36.46 bln  C$36.17 bln   +0.8</p>
<p>Wages and salaries, including tips and bonuses, make up 87 percent of total labor income. Supplementary labor income such as pensions and workers' compensation make up 13 percent.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Jean Lambert, Labour Division, at 613-951-4090, fax: 613-951-4087.)</p>
<p>((Reuter Ottawa Bureau 613 235-6745))</p>
